#
# ABox fixture for the models-and-inference class-inventory competency question. A worked
# inference scene naming one object of each models/estimation/inference kind: the estimation
# chain (a math:Estimand targeted through math:estimatesEstimand, a math:Estimator applied
# through math:estimator, and the math:Estimate they produce), the summary and contrast
# objects (a math:Statistic, a math:StatisticalContrast), a math:ModelAssumption, the process
# (a math:InferenceRun) and the plan/design apparatus it follows (a math:AnalysisPlan, a
# math:ExperimentalDesign, a math:RandomizationScheme), the testing pair (a
# math:HypothesisTest, a math:SamplingDistribution), a math:EffectSize, and the forecast
# objects (a math:Prediction, a math:PredictionInterval, a math:ToleranceInterval). The
# estimate is wired to its estimand and estimator through PRE-EXISTING edges (math:estimator,
# math:estimatesEstimand) so the scene is a coherent estimation, not a bag of types; every
# individual still carries exactly ONE asserted type so the reasoning-free class-inventory
# query returns one row per object. Unioned onto the merged ontology by gmeow:cqDataFile.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

# The estimation chain: estimand -> estimator -> estimate.
ex:estimand a math:Estimand .
ex:estimator a math:Estimator .
ex:estimate a math:Estimate ;
    math:estimatesEstimand ex:estimand ;
    math:estimator ex:estimator .

# Summary and contrast.
ex:statistic a math:Statistic .
ex:contrast a math:StatisticalContrast .

# A posited assumption of the model behind the fit.
ex:assumption a math:ModelAssumption .

# The process and the plan / design apparatus it follows.
ex:run a math:InferenceRun .
ex:plan a math:AnalysisPlan .
ex:design a math:ExperimentalDesign .
ex:randomization a math:RandomizationScheme .

# The testing pair.
ex:test a math:HypothesisTest .
ex:sampdist a math:SamplingDistribution .

# A standardized effect magnitude.
ex:effect a math:EffectSize .

# The forecast objects.
ex:prediction a math:Prediction .
ex:predInterval a math:PredictionInterval .
ex:tolInterval a math:ToleranceInterval .
